Well, I notice how a lot of the posts of any kind, even the normal,
non-YASD posts, tend to lean towards the more experienced players, and
that is understandable.  But I figured, why not take a moment to think
of what kinds of events drew us into this game?

This event-log is from my 2nd day playing Nethack, ever. (which happens
ot be the very day I am posting this)

A Valkyrie, Human Lawful... My dog and I got to Dlev 5 and I tried to
read a scroll- only to end up in the middle of Dlev 8!  So, instead of
hoping for another 'port from a cursed-book I had, I fight my way
BACK UP to Dlev 5, and in the process, I loot a couple potions, another
Tele-scroll (same markings), a wand and a ring.  On goes the ring, no
instant effect.  I am working back through, making a clean mop-up of
Dlev 5, when I find a hidden back corridor. Kick the door in to find no
fewer then 10 hobgoblins, kobolds, and gnomes- Guarding a chest, and
more importantly, an OPULANT THRONE!  Well, I throw a cursed elven
dagger at somebody, kill them, someone else dies from friendly fire,
some fuck-tard tries to equip the dagger (-2 acc/dex no-drop), and I
take maybe two hits, both hard.  I back out and fire my wand in to the
room, and BANG!  Door re-forms and locks!  Ah, 8-charge wand of
locking, what would I do without you?  Well, lather-rinse-repeat for a
while, just let the remnants stew behind a locked door, until I hit
about 16 HP after one fight.  I go to sit it out for a while, get to
20-some, and 4 rothe come down the hall!  I kill them all, start trying
to eat the corpses for regen/hunger, and of course on of the corpses
was insta-rotted to the point of knock-out.  And then a wolf came by
and ATE MY FREAKING FACE...  A valiant death, and what did I have to
show for it?  A new high score of several thousand, and a hilarious
story.

Btw, the ring was a -1 uncursed ring of Accuracy Increase, so says the
DeathScreen.


